Update the properties of a rule from a specified security group.

USAGE:
  scw instance security-group update-rule [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  security-group-rule-id      ID of the rule to update
  [protocol]                  New protocol for the rule (unknown_protocol | tcp | udp | icmp | any)
  [direction]                 New direction for the rule (unknown_direction | inbound | outbound | both)
  [action]                    New action for the rule (unknown_action | accept | drop)
  [source-ip-range]           New source IP range for the rule
  [destination-ip-range]      New destination IP range for the rule
  [source-ports.start]        Start of the port range
  [source-ports.end]          End of the port range
  [destination-ports.start]   Start of the port range
  [destination-ports.end]     End of the port range
  [position]                  New position for the rule
  [zone=fr-par-1]             Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for update-rule
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
